  "description": {
    "paragraphs": [
      "California State University, Fullerton (CSUF) is a public research university in Fullerton, California, founded in 1957 as Orange County State College and renamed in 1972. It is the largest campus in the 23-campus California State University system by enrollment, with over 43,000 students and an alumni network of 344,000 graduates. CSUF holds R2 doctoral classification and is ranked 136th among National Universities by U.S. News & World Report.",
      "The university is organised into nine colleges: The Arts, Business and Economics, Communications, Education, Engineering and Computer Science, Health and Human Development, Humanities and Social Sciences, Natural Sciences and Mathematics, and Extension. CSUF offers 110 degree programs including 55 undergraduate and 55 graduate degrees, plus doctorates in Education and Nursing Practice. The Nurse Anesthesia program is ranked #1 in California and #3 nationally.",
      "CSUF is a nationally designated Hispanic-Serving Institution (HSI), with over 52% of undergraduates identifying as Hispanic, and has earned recognition as an Asian American and Native American Pacific Islander Serving Institution (AANAPISI). The university is also designated as an NSA Center of Academic Excellence in Cyber Defense Education, reflecting the strength of its Engineering and Computer Science programs.",
      "International students are welcomed across all nine colleges, with dedicated support through the International Education and Engagement office. The campus features a 26-acre Arboretum and Botanical Garden, Pollak Library (nationally recognised for innovative programming), and on-campus housing that opened in 2011. With 31 national athletic championships and NCAA Division I membership, CSUF offers a full American university experience in Southern California."
    ],
    "paragraphsRu": [
      "California State University, Fullerton (CSUF) — государственный исследовательский университет во Фуллертоне, Калифорния, основан в 1957 году как Orange County State College, переименован в 1972-м. Это крупнейший кампус из 23 в системе California State University по численности студентов — более 43 000 обучающихся и 344 000 выпускников. CSUF имеет классификацию R2 Doctoral и занимает 136-е место среди National Universities по версии U.S. News & World Report.",
      "Университет включает девять колледжей: The Arts, Business and Economics, Communications, Education, Engineering and Computer Science, Health and Human Development, Humanities and Social Sciences, Natural Sciences and Mathematics и Extension. CSUF предлагает 110 учебных программ: 55 bachelor's и 55 graduate, включая doctorate в области Education и Nursing Practice. Программа Nurse Anesthesia — #1 в Калифорнии и #3 в США.",
      "CSUF — официально признанное Hispanic-Serving Institution (HSI): более 52% студентов идентифицируют себя как латиноамериканцы. Университет имеет статус NSA Center of Academic Excellence in Cyber Defense Education, подчёркивающий силу программ Engineering and Computer Science.",
      "Международные студенты принимаются во все девять колледжей; специальная поддержка оказывается через отдел International Education and Engagement. На кампусе расположены арборетум площадью 26 акров, библиотека Pollak (national recognition) и студенческое жильё, открытое в 2011 году. CSUF — полноценный американский университет с 31 национальным чемпионатом в спорте NCAA Division I."
    ],
